From 6a4328abdb0709bb81eeb2c1fa11c045a1f2f0ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skippy contributors <ci@skippy.local>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:48:37 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 53/53] ggml: gated delta net snapshots at chosen tokens

ggml_gated_delta_net keeps the state after the last K tokens of a batch,
for rolling back draft tokens. A recurrent prompt checkpoint sits at a
chosen token inside the batch instead, so today the batch has to end
there for the state to be read, which costs a forward pass per
checkpoint.

ggml_gated_delta_net_at takes an I32 tensor of token indices per
sequence: slot 0 stays the final state and slot s + 1 is the state after
token at[s]. A token outside the batch leaves its slot unwritten. It is
its own op, so a backend that has not implemented it reports it
unsupported instead of ignoring the indices. Only the CPU implements it
so far; the op count change bumps the RPC patch version.
